<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ran Min</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 352</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ran Min was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-chinese">Han Chinese</a> general of the Later Zhao, adopted into its ruling Shi family. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shi-hu">Shi Hu</a> he seized power in 350, ordered the killing of the Jie and other non-Chinese at Ye, and proclaimed the state of Wei, known as Ran Wei. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/former-yan">Former Yan</a> defeated and captured him in 352 and put him to death.</p></div>
